  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.Number of young male and female people included inthe apprenticeship; 
2.Number of young male and female people benefiting from the scholarships; 
3.Number of entreprenuers engaged in business incubators; 
4.Number of cooperatives established and awarded with seed capital, disaggregated by gender;
5.Extent to which partnership platform to connect young people are promoted; 
6.Extent to which communication for development is adopted.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Very limited apprenticeship initiatives and access to skill development; 
Poor business incubators; 
Challenges for creation of formal cooperatives and MSMEs;
Youth engagement is limited and fragmented;	
Limited resource mobilization for youth employment and engagement.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. 300 scholarships for profissional internalships with local companies.
2. Promote the Youth Award challenge for innovative ideas linking with SDGs
3.Establish the multi midia studio for youh engagement</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. 322 young people from Cazenga benefited with vocational training courses, representing 107% of the established goal and 60% of beneficiaries are young women, many of these young women having attended courses in the field of engeerings.
313 young people benefited Scholarships for Professional Internship Program in several public and private companies and the good performance of some candidates has led the companies to retain and integrated 41 candidates in their workforce. Internships are still ongoing, and we expect more will be hired.
2.32 young people from Cazenga participated in the Youth Entrepreneurship Challenge Initiative youth award contest and 6 of these were awarded as the big winners at the awards gala. 
3.	The Alternative digital learning initiative called &#x201c;Espa&#xe7;o Multimedia&#x201d; was established in the Cazenga training center for adolescents and youth to equip and empower them to a more effectively transition to employment and to become engaged and productive members of society.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased engagement of partnership platforms;
Enanced communication for development;
Targets will be defined in the project document;
Related CP outcome: UNSDCF 2020-2022,outcome 1 &#x201c;Economic and social transformation&#x201d;; outcome 2 &#x201c;Adolescents, youth, women&#x2019;s empowerment&#x201d;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mobilized the government counterparts in area of youth skills developement.
Attributed 300 scholarships to study in the vocational training center of Cazenga.
Support for engagement between local private sector and INFEFOP has facilitated professional internships for 100 young people in Huila Province.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
